// Title: Network Connection Initiated By AddinUtil.EXE
// Sigma ID: 5205613d-2a63-4412-a895-3a2458b587b3
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Michael McKinley (@McKinleyMike), Tony Latteri (@TheLatteri)
// Date: 2023-09-18 | Modified: 2024-07-16
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1218
// Description: Detects a network connection initiated by the Add-In deployment cache updating utility
//   "AddInutil.exe". This could indicate a potential command and control communication as this tool
//   doesn't usually initiate network activity.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.blue-prints.blog/content/blog/posts/lolbin/addinutil-lolbas.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/network_connection/net_connection_win_addinutil_initiated.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceNetworkEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\addinutil.exe"
